 "result": "The last commit is `51752b2`, \"retry longer; lower tax on big orders\" (2 files, +3 \u00e2\u02c6\u20192). It changed two functions:\n\n1. **`tax(price)`** in `calc/pricing.py`\n   - **Before:** every price was taxed at `TAX_RATE`, which is 0.08 (`round(price * TAX_RATE, 2)`).\n   - **After:** prices under 1000 still use 8%, but prices of 1000 or more use 5%:\n     ```python\n     rate = TAX_RATE if price < 1000 else 0.05\n     return round(price * rate, 2)\n     ```\n   - A price of exactly 1000 gets the 5% rate, because the check is `price < 1000`.\n   - The 0.05 is written directly into the code rather than kept in a named constant like `TAX_RATE`.\n\n2. **`backoff(attempt)`** in `calc/upload.py`\n   - **Before:** the retry wait was `min(2 ** attempt, 30)`, so it never went above 30.\n   - **After:** the cap is now 60 (`min(2 ** attempt, 60)`). Waits still double with each attempt, but they can now reach 32 and stop at 60 instead of stopping at 30. That's the \"retry longer\" part of the commit message.",
